<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-19">19 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Zimmermann Telegram is forwarded to Mexico</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s ambassador in Washington relayed Arthur Zimmermann's secret offer of an alliance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, promising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arizona">Arizona</a>. Decoded by British intelligence, its publication helped bring the US into the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-31">31 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Germany announces unrestricted submarine warfare</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> told the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/u-boat">U-boats</a> would sink without warning any ship in the war zone from the next day. The decision led to the break in relations and, in April, to America's declaration of war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/february-revolution" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/february-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-8">8 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Protests in Petrograd begin the February Revolution</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">On International Women's Day (23 February Old Style), women textile workers protesting about bread shortages began strikes that spread across the city. Within a week <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a> had abdicated.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/february-revolution">February Revolution</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-11">11 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">British and Indian troops capture Baghdad</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">General Stanley Maude's army entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> after the Ottoman garrison withdrew, avenging the surrender at Kut a year earlier. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> went on to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, under a League mandate.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-15">15 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Tsar Nicholas II abdicates</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Facing revolution in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a> and mutiny in the army, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a> gave up the throne for himself and his son. Over three centuries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-romanov">Romanov</a> rule ended, and a Provisional Government took power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-31">31 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">United States takes possession of the Danish West Indies</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> transferred St Thomas, St John and St Croix, sold for 25 million dollars in gold. The US wanted to deny the islands to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and guard the approaches to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal">Panama Canal</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-6">6 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">United States declares war on Germany</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Congress approved <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodrow-wilson">President Wilson</a>'s request for war, provoked by unrestricted submarine warfare and the Zimmermann Telegram. American troops and resources helped tip the balance on the Western Front.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-16">16 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Lenin arrives at Petrograd's Finland Station</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Returning from Swiss exile with German help, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-lenin">Vladimir Lenin</a> was greeted by crowds in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a>. His call to oppose the Provisional Government set the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolsheviks">Bolsheviks</a> on the road to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-31">31 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Passchendaele begins</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">British and French forces opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-passchendaele">Third Battle of Ypres</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>. Heavy rain turned the battlefield into a swamp, and months of fighting won a few miles for hundreds of thousands of casualties.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-15">15 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mata Hari is executed by a French firing squad</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Dutch-born dancer Margaretha Zelle, known as Mata Hari, was shot at Vincennes after conviction as a German spy. Historians still dispute how much, if any, useful intelligence she passed on.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-2">2 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Balfour Declaration backs a Jewish home in Palestine</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Foreign Secretary Arthur Balfour wrote to Lord Rothschild that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> favoured 'a national home for the Jewish people' in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>, without prejudice to existing non-Jewish communities. Its consequences still shape the region.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-6">6 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Canadian troops capture Passchendaele</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Canadian forces took the ruined village of Passchendaele, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-passchendaele">Third Battle of Ypres</a>. The British-led offensive had gained a few miles of Flemish mud at a cost of hundreds of thousands of casualties.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/julian-calendar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julian-calendar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-7">7 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Bolsheviks seize power in Petrograd</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Bolshevik-led Red Guards took key points in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a> and stormed the Winter Palace overnight, toppling the Provisional Government. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a>, so called from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julian-calendar">Julian calendar</a>, led to the Soviet state.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julian-calendar">Julian calendar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-20">20 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">British tanks attack in mass at Cambrai</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 476 British tanks led a surprise attack at Cambrai, breaking through German lines several miles in a day. A German counter-attack soon recovered most of the ground, but the tactics pointed to the future.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-6">6 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Finland declares independence</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Finnish parliament adopted a declaration of independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, a month after the Bolshevik seizure of power. Lenin's government recognised it at the end of the month.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-9">9 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Jerusalem surrenders to British forces</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> surrendered the city to the British army, ending four centuries of Ottoman rule. General Allenby entered on foot two days later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/felix-dzerzhinsky" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/felix-dzerzhinsky.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-20">20 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet government founds the Cheka, its first secret police</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-peoples-commissars">Council of People's Commissars</a> of the Russian SFSR set up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheka">All-Russian Extraordinary Commission</a>, the Cheka, the first Soviet secret police, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/felix-dzerzhinsky">Felix Dzerzhinsky</a>. By the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a> in 1922 it had at least 200,000 personnel.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian SFSR</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheka">Cheka</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/felix-dzerzhinsky">Felix Dzerzhinsky</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-peoples-commissars">Council of People's Commissars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/russian-revolution" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russian-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolution</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/russian-revolution">Russian Revolution</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Russian Revolution of 1917 brought down the Russian monarchy and led to the first communist state.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/october-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolution</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The October Revolution was the seizure of power in Petrograd by the Bolshevik Party under Vladimir Lenin on 25 October 1917 by the old Russian calendar, 7 November by the modern one.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vimy-ridge" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-vimy-ridge.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vimy-ridge">Battle of Vimy Ridge</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Vimy Ridge, fought on 9–12 April 1917 in northern France as part of the Battle of Arras, was the first attack in which all four divisions of the Canadian Corps fought together.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/second-all-kazakh-congress">Second All-Kazakh Congress</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Second All-Kazakh Congress met in Orenburg in December 1917, shortly after the Bolshevik seizure of power in Russia.</p></div></li></ol></section>
