<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/luba-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Luba%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Luba Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Kasongo Nyembo is captured after years of resisting Free State and Belgian rule</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/mutapa-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mutapa%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mutapa Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Portuguese suppress the last reduced Mutapa kingdom in the Zambezi valley</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/russian-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Russian%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Russian Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Nicholas II abdicates after the Petrograd garrison mutinies</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/mexico"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mexico.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mexico</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Constitution of 1917 is promulgated at Querétaro</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/canada"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Canada.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Canada</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Canadian Corps captures Vimy Ridge</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20the%20Netherlands.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of the Netherlands</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Pacification brings universal male suffrage and equal funding for schools</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/russian-sfsr"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Russian%20SFSR.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Russian SFSR</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Bolsheviks seize power in Petrograd in the October Revolution</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-finland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Finland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Finland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Parliament declares independence from Russia on 6 December</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-yugoslavia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Yugoslavia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Yugoslavia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Corfu Declaration agrees on a South Slav kingdom under the Karađorđević dynasty</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/rattanakosin-kingdom"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rattanakosin%20Kingdom.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rattanakosin Kingdom</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Siam joins the First World War on the Allied side</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/dictatorship"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dictatorship.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dictatorship</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Bolsheviks take power in Russia, proclaiming a dictatorship of the proletariat</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/sami"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/S%C3%A1mi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sámi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The first Sámi congress meets in Trondheim, bringing Norwegian and Swedish Sámi together</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/may-fourth-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/May%20Fourth%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>May Fourth Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">China enters World War I on the side of the Triple Entente, and Hu Shih argues for the vernacular in “Preliminary discussion on literary reform”</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/harlem-renaissance"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Harlem%20Renaissance.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Harlem Renaissance</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hubert Harrison founds the Liberty League and The Voice, the first organisation and first newspaper of the New Negro Movement</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/zionism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Zionism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Zionism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">In the Balfour Declaration Britain supports “the establishment in Palestine of a national home for the Jewish people”</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/communism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Communism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Communism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The October Revolution brings Lenin’s Bolsheviks to power in Russia, the first avowedly communist party to take state power</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/anarchism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Anarchism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Anarchism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Anarchists take part in the Russian Revolution against the White movement, above all in the Makhnovshchina</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/lili-uokalani"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lili%CA%BBuokalani.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Liliʻuokalani</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">She dies on 11 November at Washington Place and receives a state funeral in the throne room of ʻIolani Palace</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/baghdad"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Baghdad.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Baghdad</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">British forces capture Baghdad on 11 March</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-caporetto"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Caporetto.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Caporetto</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hindenburg and Arz von Straußenburg decide to send troops from the Eastern Front to the Isonzo, over Ludendorff's opposition</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-caporetto"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Caporetto.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Caporetto</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">German experts led by the chemist Otto Hahn choose the quiet Caporetto sector for a gas attack</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-caporetto"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Caporetto.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Caporetto</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On the 24th the gas attack, the bombardment and the infantry assault break through the Italian line near Kobarid</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-caporetto"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Caporetto.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Caporetto</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Cadorna orders the retreat to the Tagliamento on the 30th</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-caporetto"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Caporetto.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Caporetto</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Austro-Hungarians establish a bridgehead over the Tagliamento on the 2nd, and by the 10th Cadorna holds a line on the Piave and Monte Grappa</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-caporetto"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Caporetto.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Caporetto</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The British, French and Italian leaders meet at Rapallo from the 5th to the 7th</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-jutland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Jutland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Jutland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The United States declares war on Germany after unrestricted submarine warfare resumes</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/saint-petersburg"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Saint%20Petersburg.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Saint Petersburg</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Bolsheviks storm the Winter Palace in the October Revolution</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/thessaloniki"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Thessaloniki.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Thessaloniki</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A fire destroys most of the old centre and leaves 72,000 people homeless</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/vladimir-lenin"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Vladimir%20Lenin.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Vladimir Lenin</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lenin returns to Russia in April and in October the Bolsheviks overthrow the Provisional Government; he becomes head of the new Council of People's Commissars</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/surrealism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Surrealism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Surrealism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Guillaume Apollinaire uses the word surrealism in his notes for the ballet Parade, which premiers on 18 May</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/jadidism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Jadidism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Jadidism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Jadids found a provisional government at Kokand, which the Tashkent Soviet crushes in 1918, killing around 14,000 people</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/new-culture-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/New%20Culture%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>New Culture Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hu Shih publishes Preliminary Discussion on Literary Reform in New Youth, urging writers not to imitate the ancients</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/marxism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Marxism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Marxism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Bolsheviks take power from the Russian Provisional Government in the October Revolution</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/marxism-leninism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Marxism%E2%80%93Leninism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Marxism–Leninism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Bolsheviks seize power in the October Revolution and form the Russian Soviet Federative Socialist Republic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/trotskyism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Trotskyism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Trotskyism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Trotsky joins the Bolsheviks in July and leads the Military Revolutionary Committee that carries out the October insurrection</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/jehovahs-witnesses"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Jehovah's%20Witnesses.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Jehovah's Witnesses</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Joseph Franklin Rutherford is elected president of the Society in a disputed election, and tens of thousands leave in the following years</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-somme"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Somme.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Somme</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">British attacks on the Ancre from January force local German withdrawals, followed by Operation Alberich and the retirement to the Hindenburg Line from 16 March</span></li></ul></section>
